From bef361f1996e9c6338c9eedef3e213c121873b66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lzwind <100665065+lzwind@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:42:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hwdb: mark Adesso wireless keyboard trackball as trackball
 (#43263)

The Adesso wireless keyboard with an integrated trackball (MosArt
062a:4101) is identified as a regular mouse, so trackball-style
scrolling does not work out of the box. Add a hwdb entry in
`70-mouse.hwdb` setting `ID_INPUT_TRACKBALL=1` so libinput and other
clients treat the device as a trackball.

Fixes #29609

(cherry picked from commit bee944044f94535f4fb97740d677a3bffd040cbc)

Related: RHEL-72703
---
 hwdb.d/70-mouse.hwdb | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hwdb.d/70-mouse.hwdb b/hwdb.d/70-mouse.hwdb
index 3009ea2fdc..60a5c2a530 100644
--- a/hwdb.d/70-mouse.hwdb
+++ b/hwdb.d/70-mouse.hwdb
@@ -182,6 +182,14 @@ mouse:usb:v256fpc63a:name:*
 mouse:bluetooth:v256fpc63a:name:*
  ID_INPUT_3D_MOUSE=1
 
+##########################################
+# Adesso
+##########################################
+
+# Adesso Wireless keyboard with integrated trackball (MosArt 062a:4101)
+mouse:usb:v062ap4101:*
+ ID_INPUT_TRACKBALL=1
+
 ##########################################
 # Apple
 ##########################################
